id: pm-gh1383
title: "GH-1383: consistent SDK item/history drift reads during concurrent ordinary mutations"
description: "History drift validation can compare different item/history versions while a legitimate writer advances one item, reporting transient corruption although quiescent validation is clean. Preserve strict stable-corruption detection while observing a consistent read or bounded per-item retry."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: context-management,github-intake,read-consistency
created_at: "2026-10-03T22:14:16.447Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-04T10:30:25.219Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-04T10:30:22.191Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-04T10:30:22.191Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real isolated overlapping validation and comment append reproduces the old failure;Consistent-read or bounded retry eliminates false item mismatch;Genuine stable corruption remains a strict failure;Source and cache scans retain complete omission and integrity receipts
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: Consistent SDK history validation binds reread identity to the locked canonical item and uses a strict single-item verifier without corpus cache or workspace rescans.
expected_result: Ordinary concurrent writers must not cause stale corruption findings; changed canonical identity must fail and rechecks must preserve strict corruption findings while reading the corpus cache once.
actual_result: Both existing-target and missing-target identity mutations reject with item_identity_conflict and release ownership. Two stale-item rechecks read the real corpus cache once. The linked primary regressions and core scanner pass42/42; the full behavior/controller focus passes43/43 and six real unsafe-source variants are rejected. Node/Bun acceptance preserves18 literal transports per runtime and zero hash/chain discrepancies across152 overlapping items. Local whole-suite timing failures are disclosed; exact-head hosted complete source coverage is enforced before merge.
