body: "# Reported validation/read consistency race\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1383\n\nAn ordinary `pm comments` append can make an overlapping `pm ops validate --check-history-drift` report an item hash mismatch even though quiescent validation immediately before and after reports zero item hash mismatches.\n\nEnvironment: globally installed `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.10.3, Linux, Node 25. The independent reproduction uses a minimal initialized workspace/global directory with no custom extensions. I copied 521 first-party item records and their history into that tracker to give the scan enough duration; the fixture has 522 items including its original seed.\n\nReproduction:\n\n1. Initialize an isolated tracker with no extensions and enough ordinary items/history for validation to take several seconds.\n2. Run `pm --json --output-budget unbounded ops validate --check-history-drift` to completion. The item-history counts are zero.\n3. Start the same validation in the background. After 250 ms, append one valid comment to an existing item using a separate `pm comments <id> \"concurrent validation reproduction\"` process.\n4. Await both commands. Run the same validation again without any writer.\n\nObserved receipts:\n\n| Validation | item hash mismatches | chain mismatches | version skews |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Before writer | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| Overlapping writer | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| After writer | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe overlap identifies only the item receiving the normal comment. No repair or history mutation is needed between these reads. A small one-item fixture did not reproduce it reliably; the larger corpus did.\n\nThe copied fixture also has one constant, unrelated `_workspace` settings mismatch because its original settings differ from the copied source workspace history. That warning is present in all three reads. It is separate from the transient **item** hash mismatch described here. Neither source tracker nor item history is corrupted. No extension code or linked-test runner participates in the reproducer.\n\nExpected: validation obtains a consistent item/history read, or detects that a writer advanced an item during the read and retries that item before asserting corruption. Genuine stable corruption must continue to fail strict validation.\n\nImpact: strict CI/local tracker gates can report false corruption when another process is merely recording evidence. This was observed during an otherwise valid source-tracker quality run.\n\nDuplicate search covered all issue states using `history drift concurrent`, `\"hash_mismatches\"`, `\"validate\" \"race\"`, `\"history\" \"snapshot\" \"validation\"`, and `\"history\" \"concurrent\" \"validate\"`. Existing merge-chain/conflict reports (#599/#606) describe concurrent writes or merges, rather than this read-versus-valid-write race. Linked-test workspace settings drift (#1109) is also a different path.\n\n\n## Intake boundary\n\nThe reporter reproduction is retained as reported evidence. This delivery has not independently reproduced or repaired the race. It is queued and unclaimed; genuine stable corruption must remain a strict failure. The earlier closed authoritative-projection/cache fix pm-eax4y8 addresses ordering and stale caches, not a concurrent ordinary writer. Future verification also checks the replay/integrity invariant established by pm-hu11."
